WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:26.000
This is a journey it goes to my mother

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.120
Love's kissin' no longer

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.830
Burnin' us with sorrel

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:59.790
Stayin' so we stay

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.850
It's can't ignore us

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.570
A new world before us

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.920
Ever is

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.050
Well, you picked a hot day, mister.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:35.070
I always do. Fill her up, will ya?

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:49.760
You bet. Mighty nice transportation you got here.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.000
I'll sell it to you.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.260
No thanks. Gonna do a little hunting?

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:58.790
Well, I hope to. You know a guy around here named Cameron, Ben Cameron?

00:01:59.150 --> 00:01:59.970
Sure, I know.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.740
If you need a guide, he's your man. He knows this country like the palm of his hand.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.260
That's what I hear. How far is this place?

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.680
Oh, about 22 miles straight ahead. Then you take the left fork.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.910
I don't know whether Ben's taking on any new hunters right now, though.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:16.970
Got himself a new wife. Stays pretty close to home these days.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.680
Well, can't say I blame him. Is she a nice girl?

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.020
Awful nice girl. Pretty as the picture. City girl.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.650
Kind of a redhead, about, oh, about five for three.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.630
Yeah, that's right. Say, you must know her.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.980
They got married up in San Francisco right after...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.400
after Ben got back from Correa.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:43.080
Excuse me. That'll be 942.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.670
I have to haul the stuff. It kind of ups the price a little bit.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.310
So a place do you run?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.400
Well, it ain't much right now. Ben'll have her working for you, it's true.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.200
He runs 25, maybe 30 head of cattle. Straight down the road.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:00.420
Thank you.

00:04:14.236 --> 00:04:14.736
Did he go?

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.260
That's all, Miro.

00:04:19.164 --> 00:04:20.724
Son of a gun is real happy about it, isn't he?

00:04:20.724 --> 00:04:21.364
Let me see.

00:04:21.884 --> 00:04:24.484
I'm okay. It's just the brew that happens all the time on the ranch.

00:04:25.148 --> 00:04:27.148
Don't get so excited about it.

00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:29.708
I gotta brand this fella.

00:04:32.876 --> 00:04:35.536
Isn't there some other way you can do that besides burning them?

00:04:35.916 --> 00:04:36.856
Yeah, yeah, sure.

00:04:37.964 --> 00:04:40.084
I could tie a letter to his tail that said he was mine.

00:04:43.692 --> 00:04:43.992
Meg.

00:04:45.004 --> 00:04:47.004
I have to run out here every time I get mixed up with a cow.

00:04:47.724 --> 00:04:49.724
That bull might have hurt you.

00:04:50.412 --> 00:04:52.412
right there.

00:07:27.644 --> 00:07:29.644
I told you how to clean out the water tank.

00:07:32.972 --> 00:07:36.092
Don't get sore means your own fault. You just won't listen.

00:07:36.492 --> 00:07:37.792
I bet you will from now on.

00:07:37.832 --> 00:07:38.592
I bet you don't know.

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:47.084
Look, but that stuff dries fast in this climate.

00:07:47.468 --> 00:07:49.668
You don't hurry up, you'll need a whisk broom instead of a towel.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.570
Honey, what'd you do with that calf medicine I had in the cabinet?

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:06.220
What calf medicine?

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.640
The only calf medicine I had.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.540
It was right here in a tin can.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.830
You mean that stuff that looked like brown water?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:14.730
I threw it away.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.070
You threw it away?

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.550
It cost 11 bucks.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.170
Well, half medicine.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:23.770
What'd you think I had it there for?

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:24.430
A keepsake?

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.030
11 bucks thrown away.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.970
Maybe it'll make the rocks grow.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:29.970
Well, I didn't do it on...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.420
and I'm sorry, and that's all I can say.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.340
And if you're so worried about the money,

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.440
you've turned down three jobs this month already.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:39.670
You bet I did. I'm gonna turn down the next three too.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.300
Sure, sure, at $100 a week.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:45.080
Meg, I'm not a guide, I'm a rancher.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.260
Can't you understand that? This is a cattle ranch.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:52.090
Maybe it's not much now, but it can be if I take care of it.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.860
There isn't any fun in our lives, Ben.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.980
There's nothing but work from the time we get...

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:07.660
in the morning until the time we go to bed at night there isn't even a bath honey there will be

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:18.230
butane is a very explosive gas the safety valve is supposed to be closed when using like i've told

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:24.580
you maybe 60 times you don't close it she blows up and you've got a nice mess to clean up i don't

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.620
I don't have any mess to clean up. You have.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.710
That's pretty good. What was it?

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.610
It was a cake, you big gooner. Have you forgotten today was your birthday?

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.220
I guess I have.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:45.470
No, you never think about anything except those ugly-looking cows, and you never have.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.420
You can start thinking right now or you're gonna find yourself another filly

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.080
because this one's jumping the fence.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:56.200
Don't talk like that, Meg. Hey, hey, come on.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:59.980
Come on, I'm sorry. Look, what can I do, huh?

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:03.030
You can get the truck unloaded so you can drive me into town.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.080
Throw in some oats and some hay.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.540
Oh, I sure can pick them.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.090
I figured you'd fade in the stretch.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.750
I did think you'd make it around the first turn.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.930
Oh, it isn't that, Ben. I'm not such a quitter.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:19.600
I mean, Meg, what's the matter with this, honey?

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.940
We just shouldn't have got married in the first place, Ben.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.420
I like that. Where would you be about?

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.310
Go ahead, finish it.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:27.970
Oh.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:29.810
Where would I be if you hadn't gotten me out of California?

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.680
Serving nine more years in the penitentiary for violation of parole.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.880
Hey, forget it. I've never thrown it out to...

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:37.320
No, but it's always on your mind, isn't it?

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.480
You didn't want to marry me, Ben.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.320
You were lonesome, you were out of the army,

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:42.800
and you thought it was a pretty good caper

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.660
to get a girl out of a jam by marrying her.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:45.900
Well, it was a good caper.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.770
There was no way to start a marriage.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.560
Come on, shh. Hey, come on now, forget it.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.020
Look, I'm sorry about that calf medicine.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.380
Look, baby, come on, let's forget the whole...

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.440
Ben, we can't forget it!

00:10:59.570 --> 00:10:59.970
There was a...

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.160
I'd stay here the rest of my life, but there isn't.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.280
There isn't even any love, and you just can't live without that.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.360
There was plenty of love with the other guy, I suppose, huh?

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.400
Yes, I loved him.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.040
Yeah, he got you in a jam and ran out on you.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:14.840
Left you alone to face a 10-year rat.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.570
Even after you got on parole, he didn't show up, isn't that right?

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:17.890
Yes.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.510
If that's love, I'll take mine straight.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:23.820
I bet you still love the guy.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.850
Come on, come on, say it. You're so nuts about him, aren't you?

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:27.910
I think I hate him.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:28.930
But you're not sure, huh?

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:29.970
Oh, Ben, you don't understand.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.660
You don't understand anything.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.400
Once you've loved somebody, you never can be sure.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:35.900
Even when it's changed to hate,

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.600
you never know whether it's just the other side of love.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.160
It's the way those things are.

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:49.540
Meg, are you going back to him?

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.580
I don't even know where he is, and if I did, I'd never go back to him.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.200
Let's just put it this way, Ben.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:59.000
One man got me into jail, and another man saved me from going back.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:11:59.970
No, it's...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.320
This time I did something on my own without any help from anyone.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:04.940
Just me, that's where I'm leaving.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:06.670
Hey, please don't go.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:07.610
Ben?

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:08.430
I'll just go.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:21.570
Mr Cameron?

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:22.990
Ben Cameron?

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:23.910
Yeah?

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.440
My name is Denning.

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:27.040
I've heard a lot about you and...

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:29.710
Excuse me.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:31.820
My wife.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:33.710
How do you do, Mrs. Cameron?

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:39.090
Just, uh, what is it you want, Mr. Denning?

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.240
Well, I wanted to go across the border

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.920
and do some shooting at Lago de Zapata.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.650
Just cross the international bridge at Arivaca.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.810
Hire yourself a guide, no problem at all.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.560
Well, frankly, I was expecting to come back

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.100
with a little more than the legal limit.

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.250
I don't want to go through customs.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:56.890
I'd like to go straight through.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.360
And I don't want another guide.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:12:59.980
I want...

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:02.980
Why me?

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.710
They tell me you're the best, and that's what I want.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.080
Across the international border, it's an easy 20 miles.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.900
The only other route is 50 miles of pure up and down.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:16.840
I'm not interested.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.860
They tell me your fee is $100 a week.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.300
I'll give you $200.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.210
And my husband says he isn't interested, Mr. Denning.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:24.990
He isn't interested.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.840
You couldn't buy him for $1,000 a week, so stop wasting your time.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:29.970
Will you let me...

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:33.930
There's a lot of good guys in this country.

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:36.870
You won't have any trouble finding one at that price.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.760
Perhaps I arrived at an awkward moment.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.990
Think it over, Mr. Cameron. If you should change your mind, just...

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:48.720
I won't. Oh, by the way, my wife is driving to town.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.670
I'm too busy branding the driver. How about giving her a lift?

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.430
Why, certainly. I'd be glad to.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.150
Maybe, maybe I'd better wait till this evening, Ben, and let you drive me.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:06.130
Why wait? The man's got a nice car, plenty of room in it.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.780
Let me take that. Goodbye, Mr. Cameron.

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:16.430
Remember, Ben, this is the way you want it.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:17.330
Yeah.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:10.880
Awful glad to see you, Meg.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:13.570
You knew I was here?

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.690
Sure. I've been hunting for you for quite a while.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.100
I've missed you, honey.

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:24.570
I've missed you too, Nardo, since the day I was arrested.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.110
You were supposed to come back from Los Angeles that morning.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:27.790
You never did.

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:29.980
I know. I...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.700
I started, but I just never got there.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:33.900
I started the night before.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.980
Then I hit a truck on that straightaway, going into Bakersfield.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.060
I didn't come to for five weeks.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.880
I don't believe you.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:45.220
I can show you the records of the Bakersfield General Hospital, if you like.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:47.290
Fourteen months of them.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:51.010
You're too good on things like that, Nardo. I wouldn't believe them. I...

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:54.100
You believe that?

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:59.960
It took me six months before I could even write you...

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.340
And when I did, it came back, a dressy unknown.

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:05.650
I didn't know what had happened.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.620
I got back to San Francisco.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.690
By then, you've been in Tehachapi for almost a year.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:14.480
So I got hold of a lawyer. I gave him some dough to work on your parole.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.350
Then I had to get out of town.

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:18.690
Where'd you go?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:19.600
Chicago.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:22.500
But when I did make parole, you weren't there.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:28.080
I know. I was in New York when the lawyer's letter came.

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:29.900
I got the news two weeks late.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:35.510
So I caught the first plane to San Francisco, but you weren't there.

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:37.430
You weren't anywhere.

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:40.160
Where'd you expect me to be?

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:43.960
I know. I don't blame you.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.420
I just don't want you to blame me too much.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.670
After all, we did find each other.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.210
You do believe me, don't you?

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:04.120
I don't know what to believe. I'm almost afraid to believe anything.

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:09.980
If you pick me into town, Nardo, don't make me cry. You know how I hate you.

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:41.180
Yeah, let me take that.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:41.900
I'd rather.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:48.110
Meg, do you have dinner with me tonight?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.800
No, I don't think so, Nardo.

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.560
I have a lot of thinking to do.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.400
Hello, Mrs. Cameron. Having a night out in the town?

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:08.980
I'd like a single with a bath.

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:14.210
Ben's still working? It's 2-12.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.320
First room up on your right, and I'll bring your baggage up as soon as I register this gentleman.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:21.140
I'd like a bath, too.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.320
Take up the lady's bag. Take up a nice jar of bubble bath, too, will you?

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:36.940
Yes, sir.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.370
Sandalwood, if you got it.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:41.340
Yes, sir.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:16.570
Never know just how much I miss you

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:27.100
Never know just how much I care

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:41.170
And if I tried, I still couldn't hide my love for you.

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:50.230
I don't know, for haven't I told you so?

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:59.620
Oh, my heart.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:13.120
When will they speak your name in my every prayer?

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:15.020
You remember this song?

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.360
This dress, where?

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.270
Peacock Room, Palace Hotel, San Francisco.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:26.300
We decided to become a team.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:28.760
Ah, you do remember.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:31.390
And what a team.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:33.980
Best in the business.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:37.300
Why weren't we ever honest?

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:39.240
What do you mean honest?

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:42.000
We only took the people who could afford it.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.700
We only took those who thought they could take us.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:46.960
Nothing dishonest about that.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:51.180
Remember that wildcatter in Dallas?

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.260
Boy, what a killing.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.630
You bought me a mink coat and a diamond cliff.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.940
Yeah. Oh, those were the days.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.370
I hocked them when we were broke in Paris.

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:07.970
We weren't a very lucky team, were we?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.850
Well, I don't say we didn't have a couple of hard times once in a while,

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:19.360
but listen, honey, let's sit down and have a drink, okay?

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:39.770
Hiya, Barry.

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:42.310
Hello, Ben. I'm glad you dropped in.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:45.250
That section of land next to yours is open now, if you want it.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:49.170
I came to sell you my place. Still want to buy it?

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:52.270
You didn't seem to think my price was right.

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:54.290
Well, I changed my mind.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:58.460
One old-fashioned with scotch and a brandy and soda.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.270
Honey, I've got something big this time.

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:06.050
Bigger than you can imagine.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:09.000
No, Nardo, I'm all through with that sort of thing.

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:10.280
Count me out.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.100
But honey, don't get me wrong.

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:16.140
We've got enough to last us for the rest of our lives.

00:22:17.990 --> 00:22:19.370
One million dollars.

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:22.120
It's what I've always wanted.

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:25.410
And when I got it, I came for you.

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:28.970
How did you get it?

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:35.220
Look, sweetheart, he was knowing about my deals that got you that jail term.

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.180
I don't want it to happen again.

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:40.670
Nobody can ever harm you for something you don't know.

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:43.680
But this is all wrapped up.

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:47.040
It's okay, it's safe, and it's clean.

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:48.720
And the police are after me.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:49.400
No, no.

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:51.520
That's the beauty of it.

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:53.270
Nobody's after me.

00:22:54.110 --> 00:22:57.150
The police are after a bundle of money, but they don't know who's got it.

00:22:58.030 --> 00:22:59.970
No description, no photograph, no nothing.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:05.300
Just a big bundle of beautiful bills with Ben Franklin's picture on them.

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:12.780
That's why you wanted Ben to take you across the border, so you could get away with it.

00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:15.270
Well, Ben or anybody else.

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:20.420
I wanted Ben because I wanted his wife.

00:23:21.980 --> 00:23:24.640
For the money I'm willing to pay, we can hire another guy else.

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:29.970
It was always we.

00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:35.620
Always will be. Come on, drink it, drink it.

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:40.000
Make a fresh start, honey.

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:43.780
Your dinner's ready, sir.

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:44.520
Oh, thank you.

00:23:59.140 --> 00:23:59.920
Honey Bunch, let's drink.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:26.430
up and tell me what's bothering you, huh? It's Ben. You mean that farmer? I thought you were walking out on him anyhow. I did, but I'm not sure I should have. You know, but one for Ben, you know where I'd be now. But why worry about it, honey? You don't love the guy. Like him, that's pretty important. What about me?

00:24:30.410 --> 00:24:38.140
I guess I love you, Nardo. I've tried not to. I thought I was all over it, but I guess I was wrong.

00:24:38.420 --> 00:24:42.610
The minute I saw your face, it all came back to me.

00:24:44.930 --> 00:24:47.850
You're like something I've caught and can't quite cure myself.

00:24:49.900 --> 00:24:53.490
I'll get another guy to take us across. We'll be out of here before morning.

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:56.580
No, we've got to see Ben first, you and I.

00:24:58.960 --> 00:24:59.260
Okay.

00:25:00.190 --> 00:25:04.010
I don't relish the prospect, but if that's what you want, that's the way it's going to be.

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:06.580
Let's go now and get it over.

00:25:22.790 --> 00:25:23.210
Hi, Fred.

00:25:24.260 --> 00:25:24.800
Hi, Ben.

00:25:25.020 --> 00:25:25.600
Can I look at that?

00:25:25.980 --> 00:25:26.220
Sure.

00:25:40.110 --> 00:25:45.140
12, huh? She ain't up there, Ben. Where is she?

00:25:47.100 --> 00:25:51.730
She left a couple of minutes ago. The guy in a

00:25:51.730 --> 00:25:53.840
sports car? Yeah, that's right, Ben.

00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:59.960
Well, get your chance to do a little drinking, huh? Right.

00:26:25.720 --> 00:26:28.670
Nothing, I hope. I see your registration certificate.

00:26:28.850 --> 00:26:29.970
I know I didn't run through his...

00:26:31.540 --> 00:26:33.660
Can I see your registration certificate?

00:26:35.950 --> 00:26:38.510
Well, I've broken some traffic law, I'm sorry,

00:26:38.690 --> 00:26:39.910
but if you won't tell me what I did,

00:26:40.070 --> 00:26:41.830
just write out the ticket and let's get it over with.

00:26:42.010 --> 00:26:43.350
Well, I'm not police, I'm Border Patrol.

00:26:44.190 --> 00:26:45.770
Border Patrol? This far from the border?

00:26:45.850 --> 00:26:47.290
That's right, sir. Nine miles.

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:49.440
We cover back as far as 20 miles.

00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:51.760
Ten miles, we have quite a few spot checks.

00:26:52.970 --> 00:26:53.910
May I take a look in the trunk?

00:26:54.690 --> 00:26:56.380
The trunk? Sure, right back here.

00:27:05.050 --> 00:27:05.730
You have the key?

00:27:06.960 --> 00:27:09.120
Look, officer, it's kind of late.

00:27:09.260 --> 00:27:10.040
The lady's married.

00:27:10.160 --> 00:27:11.360
I gotta get her back home fast.

00:27:11.640 --> 00:27:13.440
Can't you sort of forget that you ever saw us?

00:27:14.180 --> 00:27:16.620
This is the only service I know of that's absolutely free.

00:27:18.450 --> 00:27:20.170
If you've no right to search my car, let a warrant.

00:27:20.750 --> 00:27:22.430
Now look, mister, we're looking for something special.

00:27:23.130 --> 00:27:25.150
We're covering the border from Brownsville to Tijuana.

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:27.200
Now get that key and get it fast.

00:27:31.310 --> 00:27:40.200
What's the matter? The Border Patrol won't give you any trouble.

00:27:40.320 --> 00:27:42.950
They're always very nice. Why didn't you want him to look in the trouble?

00:27:43.210 --> 00:27:47.050
He wants me to pull up a little.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.240
Was somebody trying to stop you, honey?

00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:34.360
I thought you were trying to kill me.

00:28:34.680 --> 00:28:36.140
Oh, Meg, sweetheart.

00:28:36.160 --> 00:28:38.800
I thought you killed him. I mean deliberately.

00:28:39.400 --> 00:28:40.920
I didn't know the gear was in reverse.

00:28:41.120 --> 00:28:42.180
I promise you I didn't.

00:28:42.260 --> 00:28:57.800
Better, honey? Yes.

00:29:02.140 --> 00:29:04.720
Looks like we'll have to walk. Rocks have busted the gas tank.

00:29:25.580 --> 00:29:28.360
Five minutes to three. Will you put out a missing person's alarm?

00:29:28.770 --> 00:29:29.470
No, Ben.

00:29:30.540 --> 00:29:32.560
You'll only make a fool out of yourself. She'll show up.

00:29:33.580 --> 00:29:34.860
Look, I've been through all this before.

00:29:34.980 --> 00:29:37.260
Do you think you're the only guy whose wife steps out on him?

00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:37.920
That isn't funny, Lee.

00:29:38.100 --> 00:29:39.720
Oh, then look, it happens all the time.

00:29:39.760 --> 00:29:41.100
Something might have happened to her.

00:29:42.750 --> 00:29:44.380
Sheriff, give us a hand here.

00:29:46.890 --> 00:29:47.710
It's Harry Castleton.

00:29:48.820 --> 00:29:49.660
Bonnie won 26.

00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:53.150
Guy ran over me twice.

00:29:53.840 --> 00:29:59.570
Had a, had a red head with him.

00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:05.020
In a pink sports car, on purpose.

00:30:07.420 --> 00:30:08.180
Come on, Harry, talk.

00:30:11.300 --> 00:30:12.700
He can't talk, he's dead.

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:34.910
Meg! Meg! Open the door!

00:30:39.790 --> 00:30:42.950
You've got to take us across now. We don't dare get another guide.

00:30:44.020 --> 00:30:44.880
Meg, open the door!

00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:48.290
And another thing. You never saw me before in your whole life, okay?

00:30:48.530 --> 00:30:50.080
Meg, open the door!

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:57.840
I should have known you'd be with him. Get out of here!

00:30:58.080 --> 00:30:59.620
I can't. My car's bogged down.

00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:02.120
You've got a lot more in a car to worry about.

00:31:02.740 --> 00:31:04.440
The man you killed has four kids.

00:31:05.250 --> 00:31:06.010
That was an accident.

00:31:06.210 --> 00:31:07.130
She was there, she'll tell you.

00:31:08.410 --> 00:31:09.490
Get some decent clothes on.

00:31:10.340 --> 00:31:11.540
I'm taking you into Aravaca.

00:31:12.300 --> 00:31:12.800
What for?

00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:15.170
So you can tell them what you know about this mess.

00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:17.360
Can't do that, Ben.

00:31:17.820 --> 00:31:18.700
She's right, Cameron.

00:31:19.260 --> 00:31:20.920
It was only hit and run, but she's an accessory.

00:31:21.640 --> 00:31:23.040
Her fingerprints are all over that car,

00:31:23.140 --> 00:31:24.480
and there's a good chance they're on the body, too.

00:31:25.270 --> 00:31:27.130
You've got to take us across the border into Mexico.

00:31:27.450 --> 00:31:28.730
All she has to do is tell the truth.

00:31:29.610 --> 00:31:29.970
I told you to...

00:31:30.620 --> 00:31:32.320
I won't go, Ben. I won't.

00:31:32.400 --> 00:31:33.120
Then you'll go as you are.

00:31:33.180 --> 00:31:36.800
No, Ben! No, please! Let me go! No! Let me down, Ben!

00:31:36.820 --> 00:31:39.280
Cameron! Go and shoot you out of the guts!

00:31:39.420 --> 00:31:41.180
I don't need any guts. I need you.

00:31:41.340 --> 00:31:41.960
You're on your way.

00:31:42.120 --> 00:31:44.300
I can't go! You know I can't!

00:31:44.400 --> 00:31:44.880
Shut up!

00:31:45.950 --> 00:31:48.230
Ben, when I get back there, they'll check on me.

00:31:48.330 --> 00:31:49.630
They'll find out I've broken my parole

00:31:49.630 --> 00:31:51.830
and I'll spend the next nine years in the penitentiary.

00:31:51.890 --> 00:31:53.090
Can't you learn to keep your mouth shut?

00:31:53.530 --> 00:31:56.560
Well, that's the way it is. The lady generates a little heat.

00:31:57.610 --> 00:31:59.410
I wondered why you married him, now I know.

00:32:01.050 --> 00:32:01.850
Well, what are you gonna do?

00:32:05.940 --> 00:32:07.620
You two really deserve each other.

00:32:07.880 --> 00:32:08.860
You gonna take us or not?

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:09.960
Then you've got to.

00:32:10.660 --> 00:32:13.070
How much would you say she was worth?

00:32:14.380 --> 00:32:17.060
Well, I offered you $200 before and you turned it down.

00:32:17.430 --> 00:32:19.370
That was before you killed Harry Castleton.

00:32:20.610 --> 00:32:21.230
$1,000.

00:32:22.680 --> 00:32:24.520
That may be all your stinking carcass is worth.

00:32:25.580 --> 00:32:26.560
Well, what about hers?

00:32:27.660 --> 00:32:29.300
Well, you wouldn't know more about that than I would.

00:32:31.050 --> 00:32:32.270
$5,000 for the whole deal.

00:32:35.780 --> 00:32:37.490
I'd say about $10,000.

00:32:38.540 --> 00:32:41.180
Ben, I'll go to jail if you don't. Will you listen?

00:32:42.050 --> 00:32:43.410
She's in it all the way, Cameron.

00:32:44.850 --> 00:32:47.850
You wouldn't expect me to put a higher value on your wife than you would yourself.

00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:49.760
Don't play around with me, Denny.

00:32:50.390 --> 00:32:51.770
I'll turn you both over to the cops.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:53.840
I believe you would.

00:32:56.320 --> 00:32:57.300
All right, $10,000.

00:32:57.830 --> 00:32:58.530
Cash on the line?

00:32:59.630 --> 00:32:59.970
I don't know what...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:10.790
I can trust you you might decide to turn me over on this side of the border you've got the gun yeah just a minute

00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:33.140
Ben, I'm sorry.

00:33:34.200 --> 00:33:35.620
I picked a trap, but I know it.

00:33:36.820 --> 00:33:39.080
I wouldn't let a dog spend nine years in jail if I could help it,

00:33:40.360 --> 00:33:41.840
especially for 10,000 bucks.

00:33:49.620 --> 00:33:51.600
Look, it's dangerous handing out an amount of money.

00:33:51.760 --> 00:33:52.640
I'd rather you'd carry it.

00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:54.590
I got a feeling I can trust you.

00:33:55.520 --> 00:33:56.640
You can keep her, too.

00:33:57.260 --> 00:33:58.260
I'm going to take you up on that.

00:33:58.550 --> 00:33:59.130
When do we leave?

00:33:59.350 --> 00:33:59.850
Right now.

00:34:01.950 --> 00:34:04.370
You got three minutes to get dressed, pack some grub and join us.

00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:09.820
What's in the bag?

00:34:11.400 --> 00:34:12.240
Change of underwear.

00:34:13.550 --> 00:34:14.390
Must have problems.

00:34:30.960 --> 00:34:44.500
Where do you think you're going?

00:34:46.010 --> 00:34:47.390
I think I'll ride in the truck with you.

00:34:47.840 --> 00:34:49.880
You and Meg are riding in here. I'm driving the rig.

00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:52.620
I don't think so. I'd rather ride alongside of you.

00:34:53.190 --> 00:34:54.770
Look, Mac, let's understand each other.

00:34:55.740 --> 00:34:57.560
From now on, you'll do exactly what I tell you to do.

00:34:57.720 --> 00:34:58.540
And you'll do it on the double.

00:34:59.360 --> 00:34:59.960
Because when you stop...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.740
When I stop taking orders, I stop moving.

00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:04.520
When I stop moving, you're a gone goose.

00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:05.580
Does that make sense?

00:35:06.800 --> 00:35:07.740
Yeah, I think it does.

00:35:10.420 --> 00:35:18.540
And the trader, the order starts to turn the lights off.

00:35:19.060 --> 00:35:19.660
And keep them off.

00:35:21.780 --> 00:35:23.290
Here, you do get some sleep.

00:35:24.920 --> 00:35:26.140
I know I can trust you together.

00:35:28.230 --> 00:35:29.030
What's, uh, what's that?

00:35:30.600 --> 00:35:36.910
Hey. In case you're interested, Cameron, your wife's behavior with me tonight has been impeccable.

00:35:38.120 --> 00:35:41.520
I'm just a farmer, Denny, and I don't know what that word impeccable means.

00:35:41.760 --> 00:35:45.460
If it means what it sounds like, congratulations.

00:35:49.710 --> 00:35:51.090
Any chance of him double-crossing us?

00:35:51.940 --> 00:35:55.350
No. He isn't as experienced at double-crossing as you and I.

00:35:55.450 --> 00:35:59.560
He never made a living at it. Whatever he says he'll do, you can count on it.

00:36:00.410 --> 00:36:02.190
You almost made a square out of you, sweetheart.

00:36:37.740 --> 00:36:40.900
A slug in my head right now would send 30,000 volts through yours.

00:38:33.130 --> 00:38:35.720
Don't jump. Don't move. You'll get hurt.

00:38:36.170 --> 00:38:39.020
Don't lift your head and you'll get an ugly scratch if you do.

00:38:39.480 --> 00:38:40.520
What's the beef, Cameron?

00:38:42.150 --> 00:38:43.550
You ever seen a knife like this before?

00:38:44.330 --> 00:38:45.470
No, I don't think I have.

00:38:46.110 --> 00:38:47.710
We use them to stick turkeys with.

00:38:48.810 --> 00:38:52.270
She slides in at the base of the throat, moves straight up into the brain.

00:38:53.620 --> 00:38:55.210
It's like peeling a banana.

00:38:56.530 --> 00:38:57.690
I've done it a million times.

00:38:59.260 --> 00:38:59.980
I hope the novel...

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.140
He's worn off by now.

00:39:03.030 --> 00:39:04.730
There are going to be lots of times on this trip

00:39:04.730 --> 00:39:07.060
when we won't be able to watch each other.

00:39:08.060 --> 00:39:08.900
Like when we're asleep.

00:39:10.530 --> 00:39:13.290
I don't like anybody holding a gun on me while I'm driving.

00:39:14.410 --> 00:39:15.770
Okay, you've made your point.

00:39:15.910 --> 00:39:16.750
Or any other time.

00:39:18.820 --> 00:39:20.680
If that ever happens again, Denny.

00:39:22.560 --> 00:39:25.620
Now we walk, most of the time straight up.

00:39:27.460 --> 00:39:29.180
I'm dumping the trailer and truck over the cliff.

00:39:30.540 --> 00:39:32.420
You grab a pack, get your stuff together.

00:40:01.530 --> 00:40:02.970
Don't take any more than you can carry.

00:40:03.860 --> 00:40:06.260
I'm awful sensed about packing stuff that isn't mine.

00:40:07.260 --> 00:40:10.200
Cameron, are you sure we can't take this rig any further?

00:40:10.500 --> 00:40:10.760
Yeah.

00:40:11.380 --> 00:40:12.540
What if we have to turn back?

00:40:13.500 --> 00:40:17.040
If we have to turn back, your buddy will have more than transportation to worry about.

00:40:17.530 --> 00:40:18.850
He'd still have the truck and trailer.

00:40:19.030 --> 00:40:20.750
I'm not leaving any road signs behind me.

00:40:22.080 --> 00:40:24.700
At the time she hits the bottom of that canyon, she'll be in so many pieces,

00:40:25.600 --> 00:40:27.040
they won't be able to spot him from an airplane.

00:40:27.300 --> 00:40:29.960
Now, look, if there's any danger of the border police getting on our trail...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.530
I got news for you, Mac. They're already on our trail.

00:40:34.270 --> 00:40:36.210
But can't we at least hide the truck in case we need it later?

00:40:37.320 --> 00:40:39.940
If we ever get in the spot where you need this truck to pull you out,

00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:42.080
you'll be a dead duck anyhow.

00:40:46.250 --> 00:40:48.090
You get out on the point and watch her splatter.

00:41:28.570 --> 00:41:29.330
that case, too.

00:41:30.540 --> 00:41:32.480
You're not gonna have time to change underwear on this trip.

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:35.140
You just take care of your end, I'll take care of mine.

00:41:35.320 --> 00:41:48.220
He never liked it anyway.

00:42:30.600 --> 00:42:32.680
It'll take four or five hours to get around on this cliff.

00:42:34.990 --> 00:42:35.910
We don't have enough daylight.

00:42:37.500 --> 00:42:40.140
We'll stay here and wait till morning.

00:42:51.870 --> 00:42:54.370
What in tarnation are you folks doing way up here?

00:42:55.020 --> 00:42:55.640
Hiya, Pop.

00:42:56.880 --> 00:42:57.780
Ben Cameron.

00:43:00.540 --> 00:43:03.890
Hiya, Ben. Hiya, Ms. Cameron.

00:43:05.620 --> 00:43:07.660
What are you figuring doing up here, son? Jumping my claim?

00:43:07.920 --> 00:43:09.300
I'm just taking this dude hunting.

00:43:09.620 --> 00:43:10.580
Hunting? Where's your gun?

00:43:11.090 --> 00:43:14.660
Well, we don't need him. We're gonna scare the game to death.

00:43:15.820 --> 00:43:17.080
Having a little trouble, though.

00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:18.360
Uh-huh. What's your problem?

00:43:18.640 --> 00:43:20.300
Well, we could save time. We had a rope.

00:43:20.670 --> 00:43:23.290
A rope? Yeah, to get these two up there.

00:43:23.880 --> 00:43:25.900
Well, time's kinda cheap, but, uh,

00:43:26.600 --> 00:43:28.740
ropes come pretty dear if you ain't got one.

00:43:29.250 --> 00:43:29.830
How much?

00:43:30.700 --> 00:43:31.460
How about two dollars?

00:43:31.680 --> 00:43:32.500
I'll give you five.

00:43:32.980 --> 00:43:35.160
Good lord, for five, I'll carry you up piggyback.

00:43:35.320 --> 00:43:36.020
You wait right here.

00:43:46.090 --> 00:43:46.790
Rock up there.

00:43:46.930 --> 00:43:48.370
I used to get hit at first try.

00:43:48.670 --> 00:43:49.650
Here, here, let me do it.

00:43:57.710 --> 00:43:58.670
That's pretty good, boy.

00:43:59.490 --> 00:43:59.970
Couldn't have done more.

00:44:01.220 --> 00:44:02.220
I'll do the hauling.

00:44:03.400 --> 00:44:04.740
You tie him on down here, huh?

00:44:05.040 --> 00:44:05.460
Okay, son.

00:44:30.160 --> 00:44:32.500
All right, Denning, you go first.

00:44:33.310 --> 00:44:35.280
Hey, Pop, tie the dude on, will you?

00:44:35.680 --> 00:44:35.960
Okay.

00:44:50.440 --> 00:44:55.690
This hole, you got that $5 handy?

00:44:57.920 --> 00:44:58.220
Yeah.

00:45:01.760 --> 00:45:03.400
Daddy, you just hold on. I'll pull.

00:45:04.650 --> 00:45:07.060
You just use your feet as much as you can.

00:45:21.030 --> 00:45:21.370
Cameron!

00:45:35.420 --> 00:45:38.920
Hey, that's... that's nice underwear you got.

00:45:39.840 --> 00:45:41.080
Man, that's a crazy color.

00:45:41.940 --> 00:45:43.940
This is what I've been looking for all my life.

00:45:44.870 --> 00:45:46.710
I'd sure like know where your claim is, mister.

00:45:47.440 --> 00:45:48.840
This even feels good.

00:45:48.960 --> 00:45:49.940
I'll take care of it.

00:45:50.040 --> 00:45:51.720
No, no, don't mind at all. Don't mind the help.

00:45:51.940 --> 00:45:53.060
Just take it easy, Pop.

00:45:53.960 --> 00:45:55.740
I'd like to have this job of the week.

00:45:56.320 --> 00:45:57.020
Maybe you will.

00:45:57.500 --> 00:45:59.660
Say, where is that claim of yours?

00:46:00.030 --> 00:46:01.770
Right over here. Come on, I'd like to show it to you.

00:46:03.600 --> 00:46:04.540
Take care of this, Meg.

00:46:11.080 --> 00:46:11.740
There she be.

00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:29.610
Sorry, sweetheart. You gotta play it the way the cards fall.

00:46:30.860 --> 00:46:39.410
He'd have told half the state, you're crazy.

00:46:40.980 --> 00:46:41.440
Bury him!

00:47:17.920 --> 00:47:18.960
You are from Washington, Captain.

00:47:28.070 --> 00:47:29.810
Tie it up, especially with this fingerprint report.

00:47:31.280 --> 00:47:34.500
The prints on Harry Castleton's belt belonged to a woman named Margaret Fowler.

00:47:34.640 --> 00:47:40.690
They drew a one-to-ten-year rep into Hachapi for a bunco job out on parole after serving one year.

00:47:43.010 --> 00:47:45.910
Their fingerprints match up just fine with Ben Cameron's wife.

00:47:46.440 --> 00:47:48.140
You don't think Ben's mixed up in this, do you?

00:47:48.940 --> 00:47:53.120
The dames messed up in it bad. That dress was found in their cabin.

00:47:56.480 --> 00:47:59.960
Ben, why not? He sold his place and moved out the...

00:48:01.040 --> 00:48:03.220
Ben was with me when Harry Castleton was brought in.

00:48:04.660 --> 00:48:06.540
So Cameron helps his wife out of a jam.

00:48:07.810 --> 00:48:09.650
After her two-timing him with that fancy Dan?

00:48:11.950 --> 00:48:13.070
That's the kind of a guy Ben is.

00:48:14.420 --> 00:48:15.420
Yeah, it figures, all right.

00:48:19.320 --> 00:48:20.540
I know Ben, and I think I do.

00:48:20.640 --> 00:48:22.200
I know just where he's gonna try to cross over.

00:49:02.240 --> 00:49:02.720
Which way?

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:03.400
The right.

00:49:04.460 --> 00:49:05.540
Why don't you take the lead?

00:49:06.040 --> 00:49:07.660
If I'm going to be shot, I want to see it coming.

00:49:30.730 --> 00:49:34.740
You a music lover, Denny?

00:49:36.260 --> 00:49:38.480
No, but I'm a sucker for police broadcasts.

00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:41.260
I'll give you two about an hour.

00:49:42.610 --> 00:49:43.110
For what?

00:49:44.240 --> 00:49:47.680
Rest. Start out again.

00:49:49.470 --> 00:49:50.710
You mean we're gonna travel tonight?

00:49:53.260 --> 00:49:53.840
All night.

00:49:56.340 --> 00:49:58.200
Aren't you pushing things a little hard, Cameron?

00:49:58.930 --> 00:49:59.910
Your wife's kind of tired.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:06.080
Carry your pack. We'll have a tomorrow for sleeping.

00:50:06.970 --> 00:50:09.690
I can walk right alongside you night and day, Cameron.

00:50:10.870 --> 00:50:12.270
I'd just like to know the reason why.

00:50:13.730 --> 00:50:16.430
We have to cross the upper end of the Papago Reservation.

00:50:17.710 --> 00:50:21.380
We try it by daylight, we'll be spotted. We have to make it tonight.

00:50:22.060 --> 00:50:26.450
Sounds reasonable. Just how far are we from the border?

00:50:29.080 --> 00:50:29.340
Far.

00:50:31.530 --> 00:50:33.050
I'm gonna take a look for the best way down.

00:50:33.250 --> 00:50:35.570
I'll be back.

00:51:04.920 --> 00:51:07.100
I'm sorry about what happened back there with the old man, honey.

00:51:07.340 --> 00:51:09.770
I had to do it. You'd have talked. You know that, don't you?

00:51:09.830 --> 00:51:10.730
Sure, you'd have talked.

00:51:11.160 --> 00:51:12.160
That would have been the end of it.

00:51:13.300 --> 00:51:14.980
They'd have picked us up in 24 hours.

00:51:15.910 --> 00:51:18.000
You'd have gone back to jail. Me too.

00:51:18.180 --> 00:51:20.740
We might never have gotten together again.

00:51:22.490 --> 00:51:23.350
We had to kill him.

00:51:24.010 --> 00:51:24.330
Sure.

00:51:24.690 --> 00:51:27.900
And the man we ran over. It wasn't an accident, was it?

00:51:27.940 --> 00:51:29.180
We had to kill him too, didn't we?

00:51:29.280 --> 00:51:29.860
Oh, look, yes.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.480
Sweetheart, the first thing that teach you in the Marine Corps is to cover yourself.

00:51:34.200 --> 00:51:36.100
You come first. It's got to be that way.

00:51:37.300 --> 00:51:41.720
It could sound like a virtue, as if it were our Christian duty to kill anyone that gets in our way.

00:51:42.030 --> 00:51:44.880
Wait a minute. Where'd you get this our business?

00:51:45.360 --> 00:51:46.500
You had nothing to do with it.

00:51:48.150 --> 00:51:52.570
We're a team, aren't we? It's never been you or me. It's always been us.

00:51:52.930 --> 00:51:54.230
And it always will be us.

00:51:55.390 --> 00:51:59.600
Don't think of the past, sweetheart. Think of the future. Think of us together.

00:52:01.050 --> 00:52:02.730
once we get rid of that husband of yours.

00:52:04.420 --> 00:52:05.560
What do you mean, get rid of him?

00:52:05.580 --> 00:52:06.540
Wait a minute, honey.

00:52:07.900 --> 00:52:09.480
I'm no gun-crazy killer.

00:52:09.800 --> 00:52:11.300
I don't go out looking for trouble.

00:52:12.150 --> 00:52:13.510
I've got nothing against Cameron.

00:52:15.040 --> 00:52:16.620
As far as I can see, I never should have.

00:52:19.840 --> 00:52:20.420
Get rid of him.

00:52:22.330 --> 00:52:23.970
I meant when we get across the border.

00:52:25.820 --> 00:52:27.720
I'll pay him off, I'll tell him about us,

00:52:27.780 --> 00:52:28.840
and that's all there'll be to it.

00:52:32.360 --> 00:52:38.010
Nardo, get the $10,000. Put it on his pack so we'll find it when he gets back.

00:52:38.440 --> 00:52:39.260
What does that get us?

00:52:39.400 --> 00:52:41.380
It'll get us out of here. We don't need him anymore.

00:52:42.560 --> 00:52:44.040
You mean we're already across the border?

00:52:44.220 --> 00:52:45.700
No, but we're very close to it.

00:52:46.120 --> 00:52:46.680
How close?

00:52:47.530 --> 00:52:49.710
Remember what Ben said about the Papago reservation?

00:52:49.910 --> 00:52:50.050
Yeah.

00:52:50.390 --> 00:52:51.710
Well, we've been there, Ben and I.

00:52:52.480 --> 00:52:55.460
It's a long, narrow valley dotted with little Indian farms.

00:52:56.580 --> 00:52:58.300
The border's just the other side of it, down there.

00:52:59.280 --> 00:52:59.980
How far would you get?

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.780
I have miles, maybe less.

00:53:04.330 --> 00:53:06.500
We don't need Ben. We can make it alone.

00:53:07.080 --> 00:53:08.420
After you've put the money on the back.

00:53:10.300 --> 00:53:11.060
Let's go, honey.

00:53:12.070 --> 00:53:14.010
This is something we've waited for for three years.

00:53:17.780 --> 00:53:18.020
Listen.

00:53:22.180 --> 00:53:25.180
We've never quite been able to get away from San Francisco, Apple.

00:53:25.920 --> 00:53:28.620
I don't want to get away from it. Not that part of it.

00:53:29.060 --> 00:53:29.980
I want to get away from the rest of the...

00:53:30.440 --> 00:53:33.140
Honey, we're all through taking the suckers.

00:53:33.240 --> 00:53:34.760
We're all through scrounging for money.

00:53:35.380 --> 00:53:38.400
From now on, it's gonna be just you and me.

00:55:00.540 --> 00:55:01.180
Get gone.

00:55:01.360 --> 00:55:24.310
What are you trying to do to me?

00:55:27.670 --> 00:55:29.690
It's good, son. I'm gonna hurt you.

00:55:38.000 --> 00:55:40.300
Nice cow! You pay!

00:55:43.440 --> 00:55:44.340
Drop the gun, Denning.

00:55:49.450 --> 00:55:54.230
Pick it up. Give it to me. Pay the boy for the cow.

00:55:55.590 --> 00:55:56.050
How much?

00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:58.480
Five of those bills you got in your pocket.

00:56:05.530 --> 00:56:06.150
$500?

00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:09.220
Yeah, we were hunting out on the reservation by mistake.

00:56:10.050 --> 00:56:10.750
You won't tell, huh?

00:56:11.080 --> 00:56:11.240
No.

00:56:12.330 --> 00:56:14.800
Here's your gun. It won't cause you any more trouble.

00:56:17.060 --> 00:56:18.600
Let's go back and pick up the gear you left.

00:56:19.150 --> 00:56:21.250
Why don't we go on across the border? I'll be on my way.

00:56:22.010 --> 00:56:23.690
How close to the border you think we are?

00:56:25.500 --> 00:56:26.980
I thought about five miles.

00:56:27.850 --> 00:56:28.610
Five miles?

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:33.180
Why do you look at her? Is that what she told you?

00:56:34.680 --> 00:56:36.120
How would she know? She's never been here before.

00:56:37.440 --> 00:56:39.260
We've got a good two days hike to cross over.

00:56:40.640 --> 00:56:41.480
Why'd you do it, Meg?

00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:45.600
Because something's happened to you, Nardo. Something terrible.

00:56:47.130 --> 00:56:49.490
I thought the first one was an accident, but now I know it wasn't.

00:56:49.910 --> 00:56:50.490
You're a killer.

00:56:51.440 --> 00:56:52.540
That still makes us a team.

00:56:53.150 --> 00:56:55.230
I do my own killing. You want a judge to do yours.

00:56:56.590 --> 00:56:59.970
Ben, I should have told you this before. This is...

00:57:00.160 --> 00:57:06.360
I know who he is. She kept her picture. Pretty crazy about you.

00:57:08.510 --> 00:57:09.410
Guess she still is.

00:57:09.900 --> 00:57:13.950
Yeah, sure. Just hope she doesn't get that crazy about you, Cameron.

00:57:14.510 --> 00:57:16.350
Because you'll watch her the rest of your life.

00:57:18.700 --> 00:57:19.940
If they've done once, they'll do again.

00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:21.490
Let's get going.

00:57:31.180 --> 00:57:57.060
Sleep till noon.

00:57:59.740 --> 00:57:59.920
Go down.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:00.860
and they will stay here.

00:58:05.750 --> 00:58:06.510
I'll take that.

00:59:03.070 --> 00:59:05.310
I'm no good, Dan. I'm no good for anybody.

00:59:07.460 --> 00:59:10.940
He still loves me, and I tried to raise the whole countryside so he'd be caught.

00:59:13.330 --> 00:59:18.380
You did? I saw anybody so anxious to get back to the penitentiary.

00:59:22.100 --> 00:59:22.480
How'd you do?

00:59:25.280 --> 00:59:26.260
He wanted to kill you.

00:59:28.710 --> 00:59:29.330
A lot in common.

00:59:32.490 --> 00:59:48.760
I'm cured of him man. There's no maybe about when your blood turns cold and you can't bear the thought of him touching you

00:59:48.760 --> 00:59:58.140
You're cured. Let's leave here Ben. Let's leave here and go back down. It's not that easy. You're mixed up in two murders

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:17.990
be too much explaining besides i want to be around when denning dies you mean you'd kill him

01:00:17.990 --> 01:00:28.500
wrapped up in this blanket you know why if i didn't i'd kill him a hundred times

01:00:30.410 --> 01:00:30.990
For the money.

01:00:31.310 --> 01:00:38.540
Not just for the money, Zee.

01:00:38.560 --> 01:00:39.720
I'm not going to walk away from it.

01:00:46.250 --> 01:00:47.800
Welling a little, it hurts.

01:00:48.580 --> 01:00:52.220
That's fine until I'm sleeping.

01:01:27.360 --> 01:01:29.630
Fever! Why didn't you tell me, huh?

01:01:31.440 --> 01:01:34.860
Come on, we'll find shell in that cave. Can you make it?

01:02:07.290 --> 01:02:07.570
Sit down.

01:02:08.810 --> 01:02:11.510
Let me help you.

01:02:11.810 --> 01:02:21.020
How is it?

01:02:22.240 --> 01:02:23.420
It's not good.

01:02:24.570 --> 01:02:25.630
Is it, is it infected?

01:02:26.060 --> 01:02:26.900
You should have told me!

01:02:33.100 --> 01:02:33.840
Everything's soaked.

01:02:37.820 --> 01:02:38.920
Hey, don't get too comfortable.

01:02:39.120 --> 01:02:39.760
We're gathering wood.

01:02:40.280 --> 01:02:41.160
You gather it.

01:02:43.700 --> 01:02:45.000
If he makes a wrong move, shoot him.

01:03:16.120 --> 01:03:23.200
have something dry to start it with that chance you got anything that might be dry it's been

01:03:23.200 --> 01:03:25.220
raining just as hard on me as it has on you

01:03:36.170 --> 01:03:38.020
All right, Denning. Give it to me.

01:03:38.330 --> 01:03:39.070
You're crazy.

01:03:39.390 --> 01:03:40.490
I've got to boil some water.

01:03:41.170 --> 01:03:42.570
She's got an armful of gangrene.

01:03:43.870 --> 01:03:44.590
Give my ten grand.

01:03:48.640 --> 01:03:51.980
$9,500. You bought a cow, don't forget.

01:03:53.740 --> 01:03:55.720
You think she'd burn up $10,000 on you?

01:03:57.250 --> 01:03:59.190
I can't believe you're a natural-born fool.

01:03:59.210 --> 01:03:59.970
You must have trained...

01:04:05.240 --> 01:04:06.000
Keep your eye on him.

01:04:45.200 --> 01:04:45.780
I'm just trying now.

01:04:46.730 --> 01:04:47.750
The next batch ought to do it.

01:04:47.810 --> 01:04:59.650
All right, then, English.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:00.780
Let's have some more.

01:05:01.150 --> 01:05:01.510
No.

01:05:03.060 --> 01:05:04.960
I'll never have a better excuse for killing you.

01:05:05.850 --> 01:05:06.870
That's what you'll have to do.

01:05:23.520 --> 01:05:23.920
Don't move.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:30.440
the rifle.

01:06:00.320 --> 01:06:00.960
You won't hit me.

01:06:02.020 --> 01:06:06.050
Just cock the hammer and aim like I taught you.

01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:18.160
Thanks.

01:06:19.810 --> 01:06:20.410
Thank you.

01:06:22.230 --> 01:06:22.710
Hey, baby.

01:06:28.450 --> 01:06:28.610
Here.

01:06:31.080 --> 01:06:34.280
You lie down. I'll have a fire going in at you.

01:06:35.080 --> 01:06:55.800
Come on. I gotta say for us, we sure got money to burn.

01:06:58.920 --> 01:06:59.660
By the way, Denny.

01:07:00.570 --> 01:07:01.630
Where'd you get the stuff, huh?

01:07:02.520 --> 01:07:04.040
A fellow I know left it with me.

01:07:04.370 --> 01:07:08.090
He was a little hot, so I held it until he cooled off.

01:07:09.490 --> 01:07:12.600
So when he came back, you just went there, huh?

01:07:13.180 --> 01:07:13.740
That's right.

01:07:15.290 --> 01:07:18.100
He didn't know you very well, did he?

01:07:18.770 --> 01:07:20.250
Oh, he knew me very well.

01:07:20.840 --> 01:07:22.000
He was my best friend.

01:07:40.720 --> 01:07:41.200
Turn off, bro.

01:07:41.640 --> 01:07:41.800
Easy.

01:07:43.340 --> 01:07:43.800
Yeah, see?

01:07:47.760 --> 01:07:49.260
Just gonna cut away the sling.

01:07:51.010 --> 01:07:51.230
Easy.

01:07:53.800 --> 01:07:53.980
Easy.

01:08:01.150 --> 01:08:01.450
Thank you.

01:08:30.250 --> 01:08:35.170
This is gonna be hot now. Easy. Easy, honey. Easy.

01:08:36.400 --> 01:08:38.280
That's it. That's it.

01:08:41.210 --> 01:08:43.430
Now, baby, this is gonna hurt.

01:08:44.560 --> 01:08:47.380
Now, you just yell as much as you want, huh?

01:09:07.520 --> 01:09:07.820
Easy.

01:09:40.630 --> 01:09:41.450
That's my girl.

01:09:42.720 --> 01:09:43.720
It's all over now, honey.

01:09:46.670 --> 01:09:47.450
It's all over, baby.

01:09:48.620 --> 01:09:50.620
It's all over.

01:09:53.520 --> 01:09:54.880
Now the back flesh just cut away.

01:09:55.440 --> 01:09:56.760
The pain goes awfully fast.

01:10:01.370 --> 01:10:07.490
I'm sorry I had to hurt you, Meg.

01:10:23.260 --> 01:10:24.460
What are you so nervous about?

01:10:25.600 --> 01:10:27.080
Just gonna go out and get some firewood.

01:10:31.790 --> 01:10:35.930
You know, if you were on a desert island with that guy, and there was nothing there but rocks,

01:10:37.090 --> 01:10:39.750
pretty soon he'd have all the rocks moved to his side of the beach.

01:10:40.490 --> 01:10:45.930
How do you feel, huh?

01:10:47.340 --> 01:10:47.920
Lots better.

01:10:50.220 --> 01:10:52.380
You'll be on your feet by the time the storm peters out.

01:10:55.860 --> 01:10:56.200
Ben.

01:10:57.590 --> 01:10:57.730
Yeah?

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:02.120
If I were to go back to jail, would you wait for me?

01:11:04.140 --> 01:11:07.360
Honey, to your little old lady.

01:11:10.490 --> 01:11:11.790
Let's go back to the ranch.

01:11:14.440 --> 01:11:15.960
You got a ranch? I sold it.

01:11:16.960 --> 01:11:17.460
Told it?

01:11:17.860 --> 01:11:18.660
Floyd Barry.

01:11:18.860 --> 01:11:19.540
Sold it when?

01:11:20.710 --> 01:11:22.590
Night I came to town to pick you up.

01:11:25.710 --> 01:11:27.930
You love that scraggly old piece of desk.

01:11:28.030 --> 01:11:29.910
No, I was getting a belly full of it.

01:11:31.210 --> 01:11:33.550
Besides, I figured it was either you or the ranch.

01:11:36.260 --> 01:11:37.760
I reckon I liked you best.

01:11:41.580 --> 01:11:42.840
I'm scared.

01:11:43.830 --> 01:11:46.150
Ben, let's tell him he can have all the money.

01:11:48.450 --> 01:11:51.420
Connie, we've witnessed two murders.

01:11:52.480 --> 01:11:54.100
He's got to try to kill us.

01:11:55.400 --> 01:11:56.600
Money isn't the point anymore.

01:11:58.500 --> 01:11:59.980
Except that you think you're going to end.

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:11.460
up with all of it well i'm not gonna leave it there for the coyotes honey you gotta have money

01:12:11.460 --> 01:12:19.720
to stay clear not that kind man what what can you do with it except run for the rest of your life

01:12:21.050 --> 01:12:28.500
me honey i'd buy you things these new shoes

01:12:32.490 --> 01:12:35.170
I'd buy you 300 pink glasses.

01:12:43.860 --> 01:12:46.340
Pardon me. Maybe I should have knocked.

01:12:54.050 --> 01:12:54.930
How's the weather outside?

01:12:55.290 --> 01:12:55.590
Wet.

01:12:57.090 --> 01:12:58.510
I think it'll take a light from your fire.

01:12:59.100 --> 01:12:59.420
Hey.

01:13:00.760 --> 01:13:02.620
That'll cost you $25,000.

01:13:05.980 --> 01:13:06.940
More than I can afford.

01:13:07.860 --> 01:13:09.440
Besides, the storm is clearing up anyway.

01:13:46.220 --> 01:13:51.500
I was just thinking what a fool I am, trying to stay awake to watch you.

01:13:52.980 --> 01:13:55.420
You're the one that has to do the watching, not I.

01:13:58.520 --> 01:13:59.220
Good night, Cameron.

01:14:01.120 --> 01:14:03.180
Too bad you can't join me in pleasant dreams.

01:15:05.400 --> 01:15:07.660
Ben Cole.

01:15:18.580 --> 01:15:19.060
Is that Ben?

01:16:14.010 --> 01:16:14.630
In San Felipe.

01:16:15.530 --> 01:16:16.810
How far away is that storm?

01:16:18.140 --> 01:16:19.160
About four miles.

01:16:23.750 --> 01:16:25.770
San Felipe is ten miles south of the border.

01:16:28.580 --> 01:16:28.760
Yeah.

01:16:32.560 --> 01:16:34.180
That puts me in Mexico right now.

01:16:35.710 --> 01:16:36.730
Since, uh, yesterday.

01:16:39.330 --> 01:16:40.210
Meg, come down here.

01:16:41.160 --> 01:16:41.600
Stay there.

01:16:44.890 --> 01:16:45.610
You think I won't?

01:16:46.820 --> 01:16:47.600
I think you will.

01:16:48.080 --> 01:16:48.980
But she stays there.

01:17:02.970 --> 01:17:04.620
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

01:17:42.730 --> 01:17:43.010
Get away from me.

01:18:01.240 --> 01:18:05.210
Don't worry. I'm not going to use any ammunition I might need later on.

01:18:06.460 --> 01:18:08.080
What do you think your chances are of getting out of here?

01:18:10.130 --> 01:18:14.100
60-40. Maybe a little less.

01:18:14.300 --> 01:18:17.690
A lot less. You're through, Cameron. So are you if you stay with him.

